<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Brydges Rodney, 1st Baron Rodney</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1718–1792</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Admiral Rodney, George Rodney, George Brydges Rodney, Lord Rodney</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Brydges Rodney was a British naval officer best known for his victories in the American War of Independence. In 1780 he relieved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a> after defeating a Spanish squadron at Cape St Vincent, and in April 1782 he defeated the French fleet of the Comte de Grasse at the Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saintes">Saintes</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, saving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>. He was made Baron Rodney.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-brydges-rodney-1st-baron-rodney.jpg" alt="George Brydges Rodney, 1st Baron Rodney" width="320" height="502" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Gainsborough · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Admiral_of_the_White_by_Thomas_Gainsborough.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
